<div class="prose"><p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p><p class="eyebrow">Hello, reader</p><h1> Hi, i'm {{ site.author }}</h1><img class="article-image" src="/assets/author.png" alt="Portrait photo of the author"><p class="lead">I’m {{ site.author }}, an author, marketing enthusiast and lifelong reader who believes that the one right book can save us from million faliures .</p><h2>My writing journey</h2><p>I began writing poetry at the age of eight, and by the time I turned twelve, more than 100 of my poems had been published. Although my career eventually took me beyond literature, that love for words never disappeared—it simply found new expressions through marketing, psychology, and leadership.

Over the past three years, I have led sales teams in the educational products industry, recruiting, training, and mentoring people whom others had often overlooked. My work has also taken me into conversations with a wide range of audiences, from individual customers to schools, colleges, and educational institutions.

Those experiences became an education far beyond sales. They taught me how people think, what influences their decisions, and how the same idea must be communicated differently to different audiences. Along the way, my fascination with marketing deepened, not just as a business discipline, but as the art of understanding and connecting with people.

Today, I am a marketer who still loves to write. The medium may have changed, but the passion remains the same—to use words that inform, inspire, and leave a lasting impression.
